      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The area that is now Lo Prado was once called Las Barrancas, a rural zone that opened the road to Valparaíso during colonial times.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://loprado.cl/comuna/resena-historica/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1968 construction began on the first phase of Santiago’s Metro Line 1, which today reaches Lo Prado’s San Pablo Avenue.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://loprado.cl/comuna/resena-historica/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Lo Prado’s Parque Lo Prado is a green pocket that hosts family picnics, sports courts, and weekend walkers every Saturday.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.traveldojo.com/lo-prado/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The commune’s name, Lo Prado, echoes its agricultural past, where haciendas and chacras dotted the landscape before urbanization.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://loprado.cl/comuna/resena-historica/",
